 {"attempts":0,"blocked_reason":null,"blocked_since":null,"blocks":[],"capability_tags":["graph","schema","spec-001"],"ci_result":"GREEN","commit_hash":"7ac4d6b","completed_at":null,"complexity":2,"created_at":"2026-09-20T19:46:05.314927+00:00","depends_on":[],"dispatched_at":null,"exit_code":null,"fallback_model":null,"fallback_provider":null,"files_changed":[],"foreman_note":"GitReins: tier-1 PASS; tier-2 PASS/COMPLETE at 1fbe324 (history 2026-09-21/b918d4ef), every criterion verified by live execution in a throwaway namespace.","guard_result":"PASS","id":"AUG-007","lines_added":0,"lines_removed":0,"perpetual":null,"primary_model":null,"primary_provider":null,"priority":"P1","reasoning":"docs/SPEC-001-graph.md sections 2 and 3. The engine reasons over relationships and there is nowhere to store them: today only decision.question_id exists and nothing populates it. One generic edge table rather than one per relationship, because DuckBrain declared tables need explicit columns and never introspect, so a narrow fixed shape keeps new edge kinds from forcing a mid-run migration. Columns: id(E-###### fixed-width), project_id, kind(opens|closes|satisfies|affects|breaks|derives_from|references|blocks), src_kind, src_id, dst_kind, dst_id, confidence(double, -1 when asserted by a person or rule rather than a model call), source(gate|impact|human|rule), note, created_at. Plus the facet table (F-######, project_id, question_id, facet(data|failure|ownership|cost|test|who_else), status, closed_by, note). Acceptance: `auger init` declares both tables idempotently and the live namespace exposes them at /api/ns/auger/tables; an edge round-trips through the declared-table API with its kind/confidence/source intact; inserting an edge whose src_id does not exist is REFUSED rather than silently stored.","review_notes":null,"status":"complete","title":"[P1] add the graph tables (edge, facet) and declare them in the namespace — SPEC-001 2/3","updated_at":"2026-09-21T00:59:07.579533+00:00","worker_status":"complete","worker_summary":"Edge + facet tables declared (COLS 11, init prints declared: 11/11); edge()/facet()/next_id()/node_exists() write path; referential integrity refused in auger because DuckBrain stores what it is sent. Merged fa6a97b. Foreman-verified independently: 6/6 criteria (round-trip kind/confidence/source intact, orphan src_id AND dst_id refused with the table unchanged, no-confidence edge = -1, ids E-000001/E-000002).","detail":{"fingerprint":"2754637efe35fd293ba9054810361edba107539c0cb6be7303ee766aff6d60c4"},"worktree":"/home/kara/worktrees/auger-AUG-007","branch":"wt/AUG-007"}
 {"attempts":1,"blocked_reason":null,"blocked_since":null,"blocks":[],"capability_tags":["graph","propagation","engine","spec-001"],"ci_result":"SKIP","commit_hash":"74abc24","completed_at":"2026-09-21T03:27:29.077390+00:00","complexity":3,"created_at":"2026-09-20T19:46:05.320192+00:00","depends_on":[],"dispatched_at":null,"exit_code":null,"fallback_model":null,"fallback_provider":null,"files_changed":[],"foreman_note":"GitReins tier-1 PASS (verdict 4455da57) + tier-2 COMPLETE 4/4 criteria (verdict af3f7ea8), both evaluated at commit 74abc24d. Foreman independently re-ran tests/gate.sh on the merged tree: ruff clean, pytest 31 passed (27+4), smoke 15/0, GATE PASS. ci_result=SKIP because the repo has no CI at all (tracked as AUG-012). Pushed 51f171b..74abc24, origin parity 0. Dispatched deepseek-v4-flash@deepseek-foreman serial on main: the 9router cmc lane auth-refused every scheme this tick, and no >=2 independent rows exist (all remaining P1s touch auger.py).","guard_result":"PASS","id":"AUG-008","lines_added":512,"lines_removed":0,"perpetual":null,"primary_model":null,"primary_provider":null,"priority":"P1","reasoning":"docs/SPEC-001-graph.md section 4 BEAT 4 and section 5. This is the mechanic that closes branches, and the engine is not one without it. When a question becomes answered|linked|moot: (a) every question with a derives_from edge from it is re-examined - if its blockers are resolved and it is now answerable from existing evidence it is GATED and linked rather than asked, otherwise it becomes newly askable; (b) when a decision is invalidated by a breaks edge, every question that decision closed becomes moot with the reason recorded, and that change propagates recursively. Engineering calls already concluded in the spec: branches DO reopen automatically when the answer that closed them is invalidated, with the reason recorded, because a stale closed branch silently reads as done and is worse than an open one. Acceptance: a question whose parent decision is invalidated by a breaks edge becomes moot with a reason naming the edge; the cascade reaches grandchildren; a question with an unresolved `blocks` edge is never surfaced by ask; a question that becomes answerable after a parent closes is LINKED by the gate rather than asked.","review_notes":null,"status":"complete","title":"[P1] propagation: closure and moot cascades — SPEC-001 BEAT 4","updated_at":"2026-09-21T03:27:29.077390+00:00","worker_status":"complete","worker_summary":"New `auger propagate` verb (rules walk + gate walk; --no-gate/--recheck) and `ask` now prints the askable surface. A breaks-invalidated decision moots every question it closed with the edge named in the reason; the cascade descends derives_from to grandchildren and REOPENS stale closed branches with the reason recorded; children whose blockers resolved are re-checked (retrieval + one JEV noul) and LINKED via a satisfies edge (source=gate) instead of asked, verdict cached on the facet for idempotence; questions with unresolved blocks edges are counted only, never surfaced by ask. 4 acceptance tests added.","detail":{"fingerprint":"0b2bcdc3ec4d732ad69d42e9f98eb91df465cf4a6c571aab6ca3293a4eb1544d"}}
